WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.300
In under two minutes, you will add an event to the map.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.336
We start on the map.

00:00:05.236 --> 00:00:08.568
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:10.586 --> 00:00:13.009
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.009 --> 00:00:15.498
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:15.498 --> 00:00:16.844
Tap Use my location.

00:00:18.608 --> 00:00:20.824
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:20.824 --> 00:00:21.476
Tap Allow.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.476
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:27.476 --> 00:00:28.693
See the three dots?

00:00:28.693 --> 00:00:29.241
Tap them.

00:00:30.848 --> 00:00:32.427
In the menu, tap Add.

00:00:34.195 --> 00:00:35.135
Tap An event.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:40.210
If your event has a web page, paste it here.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:41.610
If not, tap No, Next.

00:00:43.389 --> 00:00:46.677
Type the event's name, and choose a season and type.

00:00:46.677 --> 00:00:47.546
Then tap Next.

00:00:51.402 --> 00:00:53.422
Pick the first and last day.

00:00:53.422 --> 00:00:54.397
Then tap Next.

00:00:56.878 --> 00:00:57.997
Free or paid?

00:00:57.997 --> 00:00:59.595
Tap Free, then Next.

00:01:02.124 --> 00:01:05.244
Type the place, the city, and the street address.

00:01:05.244 --> 00:01:06.118
Then tap Next.

00:01:10.294 --> 00:01:12.572
Describe it in a sentence or two.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.510
Then tap Next.

00:01:17.897 --> 00:01:20.440
Check everything, and tap Add my event.

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:24.848
Next up: Show off your house.
